# Tracer: native Mathlib carriers with uniform Litex Obj identity.
#
# Selected ABI:
#   N/Z/Q/R/C become Set.univ over Mathlib's native carriers;
#   a domain binder becomes a bounded quantifier and keeps its membership fact;
#   symbols and numerals retain their structural source spelling;
#   target coercions occur only at checked judgment boundaries.

# A closed numeral remains bare; R supplies the native target carrier.
2 $in R

# The same `n + 1` object can have several proved memberships.
forall n N:
    n + 1 $in N
    n + 1 $in Z

# Neither membership changes the source identity of `z - 1` or `z / 2`.
# The Q judgment requires a contextual canonical coercion from Z to Q in Lean.
forall z Z:
    z - 1 $in Z
    z / 2 $in Q

# Mixed membership evidence likewise leaves each object unchanged.
forall z Z, q Q:
    z + q $in Q
    z / 2 + q $in Q

# A natural result for subtraction needs the verifier's lower-bound evidence.
forall n N+:
    n - 1 $in N

# Nearest rejected boundary (kept as a comment because examples must pass):
# forall n N:
#     n - 1 $in N
#
# That statement is rejected by Litex. A backend must preserve this boundary
# through the verified natural-domain premise; the target must not silently
# reinterpret the unguarded statement as truncated Nat subtraction.
#
# Source gate:
# target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/05_compiler_interop/compile_to_lean_numeric_obj_abi.lit
#
# Implementation boundary:
# src/compile_to_lean/math_collections.md#numeric-object-abi
